            0.192,
            0.109,
            0.881,
            0.151
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(a) If a quadrilateral is a parallelogram, then its opposite sides are equal."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.236,
            0.156,
            0.88,
            0.208
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Converse:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " If the opposite sides of a quadrilateral are equal, then it is a parallelogram. Is this converse statement true? Is this converse statement true?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.191,
            0.222,
            0.881,
            0.264
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(b) If a quadrilateral is a parallelogram, then the opposite angles are equal."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.236,
            0.269,
            0.88,
            0.33
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Converse:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " If the opposite angles of a quadrilateral are equal, then it is a parallelogram. Is this converse statement true?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.193,
            0.335,
            0.881,
            0.377
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(c) If a quadrilateral is a parallelogram, then its diagonals bisect each other."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.236,
            0.381,
            0.881,
            0.443
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Converse:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " If the diagonals of a quadrilateral bisect each other, then it is a parallelogram. Is this converse statement true?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.449,
            0.736,
            0.469
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Can you experiment and guess what the answers are?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.474,
            0.881,
            0.514
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "It turns out that all three converse statements are true. To demonstrate this, it is useful to recall how we had proved Theorem 1:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.518,
